==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Gravolo''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Gravolodon''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Use this as a tank like [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] but with way less [[Wave Attack|Wave]] damage and more effective health against [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]]. Its combination of Wave Attack and Barrier Breaker abilities makes it very effective at destroying several Barriers at once, like in [[Sleepy Signals]] or the hordes of UltraBaaBaas in [[Revenge of the Unholy (Merciless)|Revenge of the Unholy]], and for taking advantage of peons to shatter long-ranged enemies' Barriers, such as [[Le'Solar]], [[Ribbo]], and [[Axoloty]] (though the last one is a bit questionable).

Despite its underwhelming range and stats, Gravolo is still barely able to outrange some certain enemies, mostly Wave Attack enemies, preventing it from receiving direct damage from them. This can make Gravolo a viable pick on any wave stages if you have no better options.

Gravolo, alongside [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Curling Cat]], is a part of the cat combo [[Going Stones (Combo)|Going Stones]], which is a unit defense up combo consisting of two strong defensive units. Curling Cat can also be used in [[Put On Ice (Combo)|Put on Ice]], and the combination of the two gives a small defense and speed boost for all units. This can help make units tankier and get to the frontline faster, for only 3 slots.

==='''True Form'''===
It's safe to say Gravolodon is no longer a substitute for other tankers. It is still slightly underwhelming in a few regards, primarily due to the competition, but Gravolodon is as baseline a tanker for aliens you will get. Tanking aliens hasn't been done too often; [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine]] is the only other Uber in this niche, and [[Lumina (Legend Rare Cat)|Lumina]] and [[Doktor Heaven (Legend Rare Cat)|Doktor Heaven]] are [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]] with this ability. However, the Legend Rares are extremely difficult to acquire; Cat Machine as well as [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] themselves are very passive. That's usually a good thing, but Gravolodon works with its quicker attack rate. The wave attack length allows them to break more [[Barriers]], while its immunities allow Gravolodon to continue functioning when under fire from the nasty starred aliens.

Gravolodon is simply a great tanker, and it is quite a surprise that its True Form improved this much. It still does have its rivalries with [[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]] and [[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]], mainly due to the former's disposability and the latter's stats, but Gravolodon is no longer a complete disappointment.

==='''Talents'''===
As a tanker, '''[[Knockback Immunity]]''' should be the first thing to invest into, as it improves its matchups against annoying enemies like [[Mr. Mole]], [[King Wahwah]], [[M. Ost]] and the like. Speaking of M. Ost, it also has '''Target Relic''' and '''[[Curse Immunity|Curse Immune]]''' Talents, which supplement Gravolodon with a completely new niche, as its health, cooldown, and cost are simply too amazing to pass over. It's able to clear waves of [[Sir Rel]]s effectively and withstand them long enough for help to arrive. While they may be comparable to [[Sea Maiden Ruri (Uber Rare Cat)|Mer-Queen Ruri]], it has the advantages of cooldown, lower range, and Wave-generating Area Attacks to deal with peons. The stat Talents as usual, are good for a tanker like Gravolodon, simply improving its tanking and damaging capability, though after investing enough Catseyes of course. These Talents help out against fights against Puffsley's Comet and Mr. Puffington, which the former appears in the [[Heavenly Tower|Heavenly]] and [[Infernal Tower]]s, and the latter appears throughout multiple mid/late game stages. Specifically [[Misfortune in Sand]] which pairs the two together. Its Warp/Wave Immunity even makes it great for [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]], [[Infernal Tower/Floor 40|Floor 40]], and [[Infernal Tower/Floor 49|Floor 49]] of the Infernal Tower, since it cannot be chipped by Masked Grandmaster Cat's Waves nor be warped by Spiritual Yulala.

Overall, these Talents turn Gravolodon into an even better tanker with a valuable Relic niche and are great for what they offer you.

